(7032257, 1067598, 63218, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition, this is easy to look at. My eye goes right in the gate &amp; looks around at all these colors.</td>', 'Excellent composition, this is easy to look at. My eye goes right in the gate & looks around at all these colors.', '2013-05-05 11:49:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7032259, 1067029, 63218, '<td valign="top">I like the soft light &amp; smooth grain.</td>', 'I like the soft light & smooth grain.', '2013-05-05 11:56:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7032261, 1067042, 63218, '<td valign="top">This must''ve been very pretty in color, too. I like the soft grain &amp; gentle shadows. I didn''t notice the border right away, but it''s not doing this comp any favors.</td>', 'This must''ve been very pretty in color, too. I like the soft grain & gentle shadows. I didn''t notice the border right away, but it''s not doing this comp any favors.', '2013-05-05 12:04:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7032351, 1067567, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Wow, what a fabulous field to be running and playing in! The grain is subtle and not overbearing giving this photo a feel of it being a captured on 35mm film. Love the B&amp;W tones, the details, and the playful mood of this photo. Wonderful job!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Wow, what a fabulous field to be running and playing in! The grain is subtle and not overbearing giving this photo a feel of it being a captured on 35mm film. Love the B&W tones, the details, and the playful mood of this photo. Wonderful job!', '2013-05-05 15:22:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(7032353, 1067565, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier, bumping up, and coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great capture of a barren tree in a barren field. The grain gives this a grungy and old, laying forgotten feel. Even the tractor sits lone out in this field where only the crows gather in the bare branches to squawk there noisy chatter. Only one critique/observation and that is a think the grain might be teensy bit heavyhanded as seen more in the sky.</td>', 'Voted earlier, bumping up, and coming back to comment. Great capture of a barren tree in a barren field. The grain gives this a grungy and old, laying forgotten feel. Even the tractor sits lone out in this field where only the crows gather in the bare branches to squawk there noisy chatter. Only one critique/observation and that is a think the grain might be teensy bit heavyhanded as seen more in the sky.', '2013-05-05 15:27:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(7032354, 1067596, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier, bumping up, and coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great capture of action! I love how you captured the one elephant in the act of leaning over to retrieve or get something from the little gully below. The B&amp;W, and the grain, and even the framing makes this feel like this is an old photograph pasted into a memory photo album. A pleasant memory of a day at the zoo watching the elephants.</td>', 'Voted earlier, bumping up, and coming back to comment. Great capture of action! I love how you captured the one elephant in the act of leaning over to retrieve or get something from the little gully below. The B&W, and the grain, and even the framing makes this feel like this is an old photograph pasted into a memory photo album. A pleasant memory of a day at the zoo watching the elephants.', '2013-05-05 15:30:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7032357, 1067443, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love that old camera and the old style photographs. This is a great still life and the image grain complements the arrangement. However, I do have some critiques as that I think there are a few things that could improve the visual impact. First off, there is just too much negative space around the main subjects that they ''swim'' within the composition. Bring your audience closer to the main subjects so that we can see all the lovely details - especially in that old style camera. Second is that both the foreground (ground) and background just has way too much texture that it draws the eyes attention away from your main focus. A smooth, dark wood table would have been one possible choice to set the still life composition on. An old style secretary desk might have also been a good setting for these arrangement. Point is that the backdrop and foreground could be anything that did not have too much texture and would compliment the objects either by time era or period.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love that old camera and the old style photographs. This is a great still life and the image grain complements the arrangement. However, I do have some critiques as that I think there are a few things that could improve the visual impact. First off, there is just too much negative space around the main subjects that they ''swim'' within the composition. Bring your audience closer to the main subjects so that we can see all the lovely details - especially in that old style camera. Second is that both the foreground (ground) and background just has way too much texture that it draws the eyes attention away from your main focus. A smooth, dark wood table would have been one possible choice to set the still life composition on. An old style secretary desk might have also been a good setting for these arrangement. Point is that the backdrop and foreground could be anything that did not have too much texture and would compliment the objects either by time era or period.', '2013-05-05 15:40:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7032358, 1067237, 43463, '<td valign="top">Great point of view that shows off the action of him drumming from a different angle. B&amp;W tones are great. One critique is that I think the image grain is a bit too much. It feels a bit too ''gritty'' that contrasts with the bright smile he has as he bands the drums. To me the grittiness contradicts the ''happiness'' I see in the scene. Perhaps making the image grain a bit more subtle and not so heavy would have been better for the photo.</td>', 'Great point of view that shows off the action of him drumming from a different angle. B&W tones are great. One critique is that I think the image grain is a bit too much. It feels a bit too ''gritty'' that contrasts with the bright smile he has as he bands the drums. To me the grittiness contradicts the ''happiness'' I see in the scene. Perhaps making the image grain a bit more subtle and not so heavy would have been better for the photo.', '2013-05-05 15:45:10.000000', NULL, 1),
